      "body": "## Motivation\n\nNemotron VL image requests fail when callers supply a tokenized prompt through `generate(input_ids=...)`: the processor assumes a string and calls `.replace()` on the list.\n\n## Modifications\n\n- Accept tokenized prompts and expand media placeholders directly in token IDs, without re-tokenizing surrounding text.\n- Use the original text IDs for image budgeting and validate image/video placeholder counts before loading.\n- Preserve text unknown IDs when normalizing generated video markers.\n\nThe existing string-prompt path remains supported. This replaces the original decode/re-encode implementation with the token-preserving processor fix previously included in #44581; it does not change the vision encoder or weights.\n\n## Why expand token IDs directly?\n\nThe immediate 500 occurs because `generate(input_ids=..., image_data=...)` passes a list to a processor that assumes a string and calls `.replace()`. Decoding that list to text would avoid the exception, but a decode/re-encode round trip can change the surrounding text IDs.\n\n`_media_token_ids` identifies placeholders represented by a single token; `_splice_media` expands those placeholders directly in the ID list and leaves surrounding text IDs unchanged. These helpers are not required merely to avoid `.replace()` on a list; they make tokenized-prompt support preserve the caller's text IDs.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nAll **5 CPU tests** in the existing `test_nano_nemotron_vl_processor.py` pass, covering tokenized image expansion/budgeting, invalid image counts, text unknown-ID preservation, and the existing tubelet/EVS cases. Project isort/ruff checks pass.\n\nGPU/serving validation has not been rerun for this split.\n\n## Related PR\n\n**Merge first in the stack:** #44581 adds offset-based image padding to prevent literal `<img>` / `</img>` text from being mistaken for image boundaries. That follow-up is a separate fix.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nNot benchmarked; no performance claim or kernel changes.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #38953938004](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38953938004)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #38953938067](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38953938067)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #38953938170](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38953938170)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
